\\\":\\\"#norse\\\",\\\"className\\\":\\\"text-gray-700 hover:text-primary hover:underline transition-colors text-sm leading-relaxed\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"Norse \\u0026 Viking Animal Names\\\"}]]}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"li\\\",\\\"2\\\",{\\\"className\\\":\\\"flex items-start gap-2\\\",\\\"children\\\":[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"span\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"text-primary font-bold mt-0.5 min-w-[1.5em]\\\",\\\"children\\\":[3,\\\".\\\"]}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"a\\\",null,{\\\"href\\\":\\\"#egyptian\\\",\\\"className\\\":\\\"text-gray-700 hover:text-primary hover:underline transition-colors text-sm leading-relaxed\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"Egyptian Mythology Animal Names\\\"}]]}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"li\\\",\\\"3\\\",{\\\"className\\\":\\\"flex items-start gap-2\\\",\\\"children\\\":[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"span\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"text-primary font-bold mt-0.5 min-w-[1.5em]\\\",\\\"children\\\":[4,\\\".\\\"]}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"a\\\",null,{\\\"href\\\":\\\"#celtic\\\",\\\"className\\\":\\\"text-gray-700 hover:text-primary hover:underline transition-colors text-sm leading-relaxed\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"Celtic \\u0026 Irish Mythological Names\\\"}]]}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"li\\\",\\\"4\\\",{\\\"className\\\":\\\"flex items-start gap-2\\\",\\\"children\\\":[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"span\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"text-primary font-bold mt-0.5 min-w-[1.5em]\\\",\\\"children\\\":[5,\\\".\\\"]}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"a\\\",null,{\\\"href\\\":\\\"#japanese\\\",\\\"className\\\":\\\"text-gray-700 hover:text-primary hover:underline transition-colors text-sm leading-relaxed\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"Japanese \\u0026 East Asian Myth Names\\\"}]]}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"li\\\",\\\"5\\\",{\\\"className\\\":\\\"flex items-start gap-2\\\",\\\"children\\\":[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"span\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"text-primary font-bold mt-0.5 min-w-[1.5em]\\\",\\\"children\\\":[6,\\\".\\\"]}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"a\\\",null,{\\\"href\\\":\\\"#creatures\\\",\\\"className\\\":\\\"text-gray-700 hover:text-primary hover:underline transition-colors text-sm leading-relaxed\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"Mythical Creature Names\\\"}]]}],\\\"$L23\\\"]}]]}],\\\"$L24\\\",\\\"$L25\\\",\\\"$L26\\\",\\\"$L27\\\",\\\"$L28\\\",\\\"$L29\\\",\\\"$L2a\\\",\\\"$L2b\\\",\\\"$L2c\\\",\\\"$L2d\\\",\\\"$L2e\\\",\\\"$L2f\\\",\\\"$L30\\\",\\\"$L31\\\",\\\"$L32\\\",\\\"$L33\\\",\\\"$L34\\\",\\\"$L35\\\",\\\"$L36\\\"]}],\\\"$L37\\\",\\\"$L38\\\",\\\"$L39\\\",\\\"$L3a\\\",\\\"$L3b\\\",\\\"$L3c\\\"]}]\\n\"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,\"23:[\\\"$\\\",\\\"li\\\",\\\"6\\\",{\\\"className\\\":\\\"flex items-start gap-2\\\",\\\"children\\\":[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"span\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"text-primary font-bold mt-0.5 min-w-[1.5em]\\\",\\\"children\\\":[7,\\\".\\\"]}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"a\\\",null,{\\\"href\\\":\\\"#faq\\\",\\\"className\\\":\\\"text-gray-700 hover:text-primary hover:underline transition-colors text-sm leading-relaxed\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"FAQ\\\"}]]}]\\n24:[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",\\\"1\\\",{\\\"className\\\":\\\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\\\",\\\"children\\\":[\\\"Mythology offers some of the richest, most meaningful names you can give a pet. These names carry thousands of years of storytelling, power, and cultural significance. Whether you choose a Greek god for a majestic \\\",[\\\"$\\\",\\\"$L3\\\",\\\"214\\\",{\\\"href\\\":\\\"/animal/dog/\\\",\\\"className\\\":\\\"text-primary font-semibold hover:underline\\\",\\\"children\\\":[\\\"Dog\\\",\\\" Name Generator\\\"]}],\\\", a Norse hero for a brave \\\",[\\\"$\\\",\\\"$L3\\\",\\\"246\\\",{\\\"href\\\":\\\"/animal/cat/\\\",\\\"className\\\":\\\"text-primary font-semibold hover:underline\\\",\\\"children\\\":[\\\"Cat\\\",\\\" Name Generator\\\"]}],\\\", or a mythical creature for a magical \\\",[\\\"$\\\",\\\"$L3\\\",\\\"290\\\",{\\\"href\\\":\\\"/animal/dragon/\\\",\\\"className\\\":\\\"text-primary font-semibold hover:underline\\\",\\\"children\\\":[\\\"Dragon\\\",\\\" Name Generator\\\"]}],\\\", mythological names make every call of your pet's name feel epic. Whether you're naming a powerful earthworm or a graceful alpaca, mythological names add depth and story to every call.\\\"]}]\\n25:[\\\"$\\\",\\\"h2\\\",\\\"2\\\",{\\\"className\\\":\\\"text-2xl font-bold mt-10 mb-4 text-gray-900\\\",\\\"children\\\":[\\\"Greek Mythology Animal Names 🏛️\\\"]}]\\n26:[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",\\\"3\\\",{\\\"className\\\":\\\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\\\",\\\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\\\":{\\\"__html\\\":\\\"Greek mythology offers an unmatched treasury of powerful names. \\u003cstrong\\u003eZeus\\u003c/strong\\u003e, king of the gods, is perfect for a commanding pet. \\u003cstrong\\u003eAthena\\u003c/strong\\u003e, goddess of wisdom, suits an intelligent companion. \\u003cstrong\\u003eApollo\\u003c/strong\\u003e, god of the sun and arts, shines for a radiant pet. Other favorites include \\u003cstrong\\u003eAres\\u003c/strong\\u003e (war), \\u003cstrong\\u003eHera\\u003c/strong\\u003e (queen of gods), \\u003cstrong\\u003eHermes\\u003c/strong\\u003e (messenger), \\u003cstrong\\u003eArtemis\\u003c/strong\\u003e (huntress), and \\u003cstrong\\u003ePersephone\\u003c/strong\\u003e (spring). These names work wonderfully for breeds like bobcat, hammerhead-shark, and sea-lily.\\\"}}]\\n27:[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",\\\"4\\\",{\\\"className\\\":\\\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\\\",\\\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\\\":{\\\"__html\\\":\\\"For lesser-known but equally beautiful options, consider \\u003cstrong\\u003eNyx\\u003c/strong\\u003e (night), \\u003cstrong\\u003eEos\\u003c/strong\\u003e (dawn), \\u003cstrong\\u003eSelene\\u003c/strong\\u003e (moon), \\u003cstrong\\u003eHelios\\u003c/strong\\u003e (sun), \\u003cstrong\\u003eNike\\u003c/strong\\u003e (victory), or \\u003cstrong\\u003eIris\\u003c/strong\\u003e (rainbow). Titan names bring ancient power: \\u003cstrong\\u003eAtlas\\u003c/strong\\u003e, \\u003cstrong\\u003ePrometheus\\u003c/strong\\u003e, \\u003cstrong\\u003eOceanus\\u003c/strong\\u003e, \\u003cstrong\\u003eHyperion\\u003c/strong\\u003e. For a {bird}, \\u003cstrong\\u003eZephyr\\u003c/strong\\u003e (west wind) is a lyrical choice.\\\"}}]\\n28:[\\\"$\\\",\\\"h2\\\",\\\"5\\\",{\\\"className\\\":\\\"text-2xl font-bold mt-10 mb-4 text-gray-900\\\",\\\"children\\\":[\\\"Norse \\u0026 Viking Animal Names ⚔️\\\"]}]\\n29:[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",\\\"6\\\",{\\\"className\\\":\\\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\\\",\\\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\\\":{\\\"__html\\\":\\\"Norse mythology provides bold, strong names ideal for powerful pets. \\u003cstrong\\u003eThor\\u003c/strong\\u003e, god of thunder, remains one of the most popular mythological pet names. \\u003cstrong\\u003eOdin\\u003c/strong\\u003e, the All-Father, suits a wise and watchful companion. \\u003cstrong\\u003eFreya\\u003c/strong\\u003e, goddess of love and war, works beautifully for a {cat} with dual nature. \\u003cstrong\\u003eLoki\\u003c/strong\\u003e, the trickster, is perfect for mischievous pets.\\\"}}]\\n2a:[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",\\\"7\\\",{\\\"className\\\":\\\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\\\",\\\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\\\":{\\\"__html\\\":\\\"Other Norse gems: \\u003cstrong\\u003eTyr\\u003c/strong\\u003e (god of war), \\u003cstrong\\u003eBalder\\u003c/strong\\u003e (god of light), \\u003cstrong\\u003eHeimdall\\u003c/strong\\u003e (guardian of Bifrost), \\u003cstrong\\u003eSkadi\\u003c/strong\\u003e (winter goddess), \\u003cstrong\\u003eIdunn\\u003c/strong\\u003e (goddess of youth), \\u003cstrong\\u003eFrigg\\u003c/strong\\u003e (queen of Asgard). The great wolf \\u003cstrong\\u003eFenrir\\u003c/strong\\u003e and world serpent \\u003cstrong\\u003eJormungandr\\u003c/strong\\u003e make intense names for large pets. \\u003cstrong\\u003eValkyrie\\u003c/strong\\u003e brings warrior spirit, while \\u003cstrong\\u003eYggdrasil\\u003c/strong\\u003e, the world tree, connects to all life.\\\"}}]\\n2b:[\\\"$\\\",\\\"h2\\\",\\\"8\\\",{\\\"className\\\":\\\"text-2xl font-bold mt-10 mb-4 text-gray-900\\\",\\\"children\\\":[\\\"Egyptian Mythology Animal Names 𓂀\\\"]}]\\n2c:[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",\\\"9\\\",{\\\"className\\\":\"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,\"\\\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\\\",\\\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\\\":{\\\"__html\\\":\\\"Ancient Egypt revered animals, making Egyptian mythology especially fitting for pet names. \\u003cstrong\\u003eBastet\\u003c/strong\\u003e, the cat goddess, is the ultimate feline namesake. \\u003cstrong\\u003eAnubis\\u003c/strong\\u003e, the jackal-headed god, suits a loyal {dog}. \\u003cstrong\\u003eRa\\u003c/strong\\u003e, the sun god, and \\u003cstrong\\u003eHorus\\u003c/strong\\u003e, the falcon god, bring sky power. \\u003cstrong\\u003eIsis\\u003c/strong\\u003e and \\u003cstrong\\u003eOsiris\\u003c/strong\\u003e carry profound mythological weight.\\\"}}]\\n2d:[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",\\\"10\\\",{\\\"className\\\":\\\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\\\",\\\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\\\":{\\\"__html\\\":\\\"Egyptian names rich with meaning: \\u003cstrong\\u003eSekhmet\\u003c/strong\\u003e (lioness goddess), \\u003cstrong\\u003eThoth\\u003c/strong\\u003e (god of wisdom), \\u003cstrong\\u003eSobek\\u003c/strong\\u003e (crocodile god), \\u003cstrong\\u003eWadjet\\u003c/strong\\u003e (cobra goddess), \\u003cstrong\\u003eNephthys\\u003c/strong\\u003e, \\u003cstrong\\u003eHathor\\u003c/strong\\u003e (goddess of love). Place names like \\u003cstrong\\u003eCairo\\u003c/strong\\u003e, \\u003cstrong\\u003eLuxor\\u003c/strong\\u003e, \\u003cstrong\\u003eNubia\\u003c/strong\\u003e, and \\u003cstrong\\u003eNile\\u003c/strong\\u003e bring Egyptian geography. The \\u003cstrong\\u003eSphinx\\u003c/strong\\u003e and \\u003cstrong\\u003ephoenix\\u003c/strong\\u003e offer mythical creature connections.\\\"}}]\\n2e:[\\\"$\\\",\\\"h2\\\",\\\"11\\\",{\\\"className\\\":\\\"text-2xl font-bold mt-10 mb-4 text-gray-900\\\",\\\"children\\\":[\\\"Celtic \\u0026 Irish Mythological Names 🍀\\\"]}]\\n2f:[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",\\\"12\\\",{\\\"className\\\":\\\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\\\",\\\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\\\":{\\\"__html\\\":\\\"Celtic mythology offers lyrical, nature-connected names perfect for pets. \\u003cstrong\\u003eFinn\\u003c/strong\\u003e (fair hero), \\u003cstrong\\u003eBrigid\\u003c/strong\\u003e (goddess of poetry), \\u003cstrong\\u003eLugh\\u003c/strong\\u003e (god of skills), \\u003cstrong\\u003eMorrigan\\u003c/strong\\u003e (phantom queen), and \\u003cstrong\\u003eDagda\\u003c/strong\\u003e (good god) bring Irish legend to life.\\\"}}]\\n30:[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",\\\"13\\\",{\\\"className\\\":\\\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\\\",\\\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\\\":{\\\"__html\\\":\\\"Magical Celtic names: \\u003cstrong\\u003eAine\\u003c/strong\\u003e (fairy queen), \\u003cstrong\\u003eFionnuala\\u003c/strong\\u003e (white shoulder), \\u003cstrong\\u003eOisin\\u003c/strong\\u003e (little deer), \\u003cstrong\\u003eNiamh\\u003c/strong\\u003e (bright), \\u003cstrong\\u003eCian\\u003c/strong\\u003e (ancient). Arthurian names add medieval legend: \\u003cstrong\\u003eArthur\\u003c/strong\\u003e, \\u003cstrong\\u003eGuinevere\\u003c/strong\\u003e, \\u003cstrong\\u003eMerlin\\u003c/strong\\u003e, \\u003cstrong\\u003eMorgana\\u003c/strong\\u003e, \\u003cstrong\\u003eLancelot\\u003c/strong\\u003e, \\u003cstrong\\u003eNimue\\u003c/strong\\u003e (Lady of the Lake).\\\"}}]\\n31:[\\\"$\\\",\\\"h2\\\",\\\"14\\\",{\\\"className\\\":\\\"text-2xl font-bold mt-10 mb-4 text-gray-900\\\",\\\"children\\\":[\\\"Japanese \\u0026 East Asian Myth Names ⛩️\\\"]}]\\n32:[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",\\\"15\\\",{\\\"className\\\":\\\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\\\",\\\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\\\":{\\\"__html\\\":\\\"Japanese mythology provides elegant, nature-connected names. \\u003cstrong\\u003eAmaterasu\\u003c/strong\\u003e, the sun goddess, brings radiant energy. \\u003cstrong\\u003eRaijin\\u003c/strong\\u003e (thunder god) and \\u003cstrong\\u003eFujin\\u003c/strong\\u003e (wind god) suit stormy pets. \\u003cstrong\\u003eKitsune\\u003c/strong\\u003e, the fox spirit, is perfect for clever pets. \\u003cstrong\\u003eRyujin\\u003c/strong\\u003e, the dragon sea god, works for aquatic animals.\\\"}}]\\n33:[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",\\\"16\\\",{\\\"className\\\":\\\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\\\",\\\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\\\":{\\\"__html\\\":\\\"Chinese mythology offers \\u003cstrong\\u003eLong\\u003c/strong\\u003e (dragon), \\u003cstrong\\u003eFenghuang\\u003c/strong\\u003e (phoenix), \\u003cstrong\\u003eQilin\\u003c/strong\\u003e (unicorn-like chimera). Japanese kami (spirit) names are poetic: \\u003cstrong\\u003eSakura\\u003c/strong\\u003e (cherry blossom), \\u003cstrong\\u003eTsukuyomi\\u003c/strong\\u003e (moon god), \\u003cstrong\\u003eInari\\u003c/strong\\u003e (rice and fox god), \\u003cstrong\\u003eSusanoo\\u003c/strong\\u003e (storm god).\\\"}}]\\n34:[\\\"$\\\",\\\"h2\\\",\\\"17\\\",{\\\"className\\\":\\\"text-2xl font-bold mt-10 mb-4 text-gray-900\\\",\\\"children\\\":[\\\"Mythical Creature Names 🐉\\\"]}]\\n35:[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",\\\"18\\\",{\\\"className\\\":\\\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\\\",\\\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\\\":{\\\"__html\\\":\\\"Mythical creatures themselves make wonderful pet names. \\u003cstrong\\u003eDragon\\u003c/strong\\u003e, \\u003cstrong\\u003ePhoenix\\u003c/strong\\u003e, \\u003cstrong\\u003eGriffin\\u003c/strong\\u003e, \\u003cstrong\\u003ePegasus\\u003c/strong\\u003e, \\u003cstrong\\u003eUnicorn\\u003c/strong\\u003e — these names carry magic. Less common creature names: \\u003cstrong\\u003eBasilisk\\u003c/strong\\u003e, \\u003cstrong\\u003eChimera\\u003c/strong\\u003e, \\u003cstrong\\u003eHydra\\u003c/strong\\u003e, \\u003cstrong\\u003eManticore\\u003c/strong\\u003e, \\u003cstrong\\u003eHippogriff\\u003c/strong\\u003e. For lighter options, \\u003cstrong\\u003eFairy\\u003c/strong\\u003e, \\u003cstrong\\u003ePixie\\u003c/strong\\u003e, \\u003cstrong\\u003eSprite\\u003c/strong\\u003e, \\u003cstrong\\u003eElf\\u003c/strong\\u003e, \\u003cstrong\\u003eGnome\\u003c/strong\\u003e bring woodland magic.\\\"}}]\\n36:[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",\\\"19\\\",{\\\"className\\\":\\\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\\\",\\\"children\\\":[\\\"Explore more \"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,\"naming inspiration across our site: megamouth-shark, regal-tang, exquisite-wrasse, narwhal, grison, and hundreds of other animal name generators — all free and carefully curated by our editorial team.\\\"]}]\\n\"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,\"37:[\\\"$\\\",\\\"section\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"mt-12 bg-white rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100\\\",\\\"children\\\":[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"h2\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"text-2xl font-bold mb-6\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"❓ Frequently Asked Questions\\\"}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"div\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"space-y-3\\\",\\\"children\\\":[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"details\\\",\\\"0\\\",{\\\"className\\\":\\\"bg-gray-50 rounded-xl p-5 group\\\",\\\"children\\\":[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"summary\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"font-semibold cursor-pointer group-open:text-primary\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"Are mythological names too serious for pets?\\\"}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"mt-3 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"Not at all! Mythological names can be as playful or serious as you make them. A tiny hamster named Zeus creates wonderful irony, while a majestic dog named Athena feels entirely appropriate. The contrast between name and pet often creates the most endearing combinations.\\\"}]]}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"details\\\",\\\"1\\\",{\\\"className\\\":\\\"bg-gray-50 rounded-xl p-5 group\\\",\\\"children\\\":[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"summary\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"font-semibold cursor-pointer group-open:text-primary\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"Should I consider the god's story when choosing a name?\\\"}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"mt-3 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"It helps to know the basic mythology to ensure the association feels right. A trickster pet suits Loki perfectly, while a calm, wise pet might be better as Athena. But don't overthink it — the name should feel good to you first.\\\"}]]}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"details\\\",\\\"2\\\",{\\\"className\\\":\\\"bg-gray-50 rounded-xl p-5 group\\\",\\\"children\\\":[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"summary\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"font-semibold cursor-pointer group-open:text-primary\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"What culture's mythology works best for pet names?\\\"}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"mt-3 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"Greek and Norse mythologies are most popular in Western countries because the names are familiar and pronounceable. However, exploring mythologies from around the world can uncover truly unique, meaningful names.\\\"}]]}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"details\\\",\\\"3\\\",{\\\"className\\\":\\\"bg-gray-50 rounded-xl p-5 group\\\",\\\"children\\\":[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"summary\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"font-semibold cursor-pointer group-open:text-primary\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"Can I use the name of a villainous mythological figure?\\\"}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"mt-3 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"Absolutely! Villain names like Loki, Hades, Medusa, and Circe often make the most memorable pet names. They carry charisma and complexity that make them endlessly interesting.\\\"}]]}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"details\\\",\\\"4\\\",{\\\"className\\\":\\\"bg-gray-50 rounded-xl p-5 group\\\",\\\"children\\\":[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"summary\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"font-semibold cursor-pointer group-open:text-primary\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"Are mythological names good for all types of pets?\\\"}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"mt-3 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"Yes — mythological names work beautifully across species. A tiny hamster named Zeus has wonderful ironic charm, while a majestic Great Dane named Athena feels perfectly fitting. For dogs, strong Norse names excel; for cats, elegant Egyptian names shine; for birds, airy Greek names feel natural. Match the mythology to your pet's personality, not their size.\\\"}]]}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"details\\\",\\\"5\\\",{\\\"className\\\":\\\"bg-gray-50 rounded-xl p-5 group\\\",\\\"children\\\":[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"summary\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"font-semibold cursor-pointer group-open:text-primary\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"Which mythological names are currently trending?\\\"}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"mt-3 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"In 2024-2026, Loki remains the top trending mythological pet name, followed by Athena, Apollo, Freya, and Thor. Phoenix has surged for rescue pets. For cats, Bastet and Cleo are popular Egyptian-inspired choices. Among more unique options, Nyx, Circe, Zephyr, and Persephone are gaining traction among pet owners seeking distinctive mythological names.\\\"}]]}],\\\"$L3d\\\"]}]]}]\\n\"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,\"38:[\\\"$\\\",\\\"section\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"mt-12\\\",\\\"children\\\":[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"h2\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"text-2xl font-bold mb-6\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"🐾 Related Animal Name Generators\\\"}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"div\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"grid grid-cols-2 sm:grid-cols-3 md:grid-cols-4 gap-3\\\",\\\"children\\\":[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"$L3\\\",\\\"dragon\\\",{\\\"href\\\":\\\"/animal/dragon/\\\",\\\"className\\\":\\\"bg-white rounded-xl p-4 text-center border border-gray-100 shadow-sm hover:shadow-md hover:border-primary/30 transition-all group\\\",\\\"children\\\":[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"div\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"text-2xl mb-1\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"🐉\\\"}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"div\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"text-sm font-semibold text-gray-700 group-hover:text-primary\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"Dragon\\\"}]]}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"$L3\\\",\\\"unicorn\\\",{\\\"href\\\":\\\"/animal/unicorn/\\\",\\\"className\\\":\\\"bg-white